apex Legends season four assimilation  has arrived bringing a new legend weapon  battle past map changes and more here's  everything you need to know to  assimilate yourself into the new season  let's talk about revenant first the Robo  killer has joined the apex games and  he's bringing a literally deadly  combination of abilities to the  competition revenant is an assassin and  his abilities reflect that his passive  called stalker lets him Crouch walk  faster and climb walls higher than other  characters his tactical is called  silence and it's a throne device that  damages the enemy and temporarily  disables their own abilities  finally there's his ultimate death totem  this keeps your teammates alive for a  limited time if they die they'll simply  respawn at the totem ready for more  action  revenant isn't unkillable however his  low profile trait means that he takes an  extra 5% damage if you're not able to  pick revenant for your squad right away  don't worry you should still be able to  find the new weapon The Sentinel this  sniper rifle has a unique mechanic  compared to others in the game you can  switch your fire to an energized state  while powered on the Sentinel fires  special projectiles that deal extra  damage to shields these projectiles  leave trails and make a unique sound so  other players will know the Sentinel has  been powered up to activate this  energized state you'll need to give up  one shield battery in your inventory and  the effect will only last for 90 seconds  along with a new sniper comes sniper  ammo up until this point  snipers SMGs and LMGs all use the same  ammo but respawn is changing that now  you'll find unique sniper ammo for the  longbow triple take charge rifle and a  new Sentinel note that the g7 is missing  from this list it's now an assault rifle  instead of course you can also deck out  the Sentinel and other weapons with new  battle pass rewards as usual the  assimilation battle Pass includes 100  levels of rewards to unlock but you'll  get some bonuses just for picking it up  buying the pass gets you epic skins for  Pathfinder lifeline and crypto plus a  legendary skin for the r99  the Battle Pass will cost you nine  hundred and fifty apex coins but you can  also grab a bundle for twenty eight  hundred coins that automatically unlocks  the first 25 levels of rewards and Nets  you the perfect soldier skin for Wraith  if you don't want to spend money that's  cool to anyone who plays season four can  still earn five apex packs and caustics  cyber sludge skin now let's talk about  map changes world's edge is getting a  fresh coat of paint and some key spots  first up is the planet harvester which  has been dropped smack dab in the middle  of the map the harvester is a massive  structure full of close quarters  hallways and corners to battle in the  harvester has also calls capital city to  split in half with one chunk to the west  one to the east with a volcanic fissure  between good news if you fall into the  pit you won't immediately die bad news  you will take 25 damage every time you  fall in and the warm wind will carry you  to safety very very slowly making you a  pretty open target lastly there's an  all-new spot called the survey camp if  you check it out you'll actually find  racks of weapons inside some of the  buildings if all of this has you itching  to jump back into ranked mode then  there's one more thing you need to know  much like capital city it's being split  in two this season from now through  March 23rd you'll be battling and  ranking up on world's edge for March  24th through May 5th you'll move to  Kings Canyon and start ranking up from  scratch to different rank series means  two sets of rewards plus bonus animated  badges for top players on both Maps  season 4 comes alongside a new update  bringing weapon balance changes and  quality of life improvements on top of  everything we talked about here so be  sure to check out the full patch notes  on gamespot stay tuned for our upcoming  revenant legend guide and tons more  assimilation coverage we'll see you in  the apex games  [Music]
 

